                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 6,
                            "playtime_at_review": 204,
                            "last_played": 1792963553
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "After playing the game for a bit, here is my review.\n\nDig Dug was a very old game, it came out in 1982 and it was a success. I had this conversation with my dad and he told me about the good times he had playing Dig Dug (he is old lol). This port of the game for steam was pretty cool. Even though you will be able to play Dig Dug for free on a browser or something, it worked out pretty cool on Steam. One thing that caught my eye was the game had achievements, which I thought was sick for a port of Dig Dug. I love to collect steam achievements because it is soo satisfying after you 100% a game so to me, the fact it had achievements was SICK! The price was a tad bit expensive especially for a $4 port of a game that can easily be played on a browser, I feel like they could've toned it down to at least $2. Overall, a pretty cool port, I do like the pause screen and the designs. It's pretty cool\n\nI would give it a solid 7/10",
